Quick bit of Python to programmatically convert a Mode S / ADS-B address into an Australian VH- ICAO registration.

Licensed under the MIT License - see the LICENSE file for the full text.
Copyright (c) 2021-2026 Matt Ames and Matt Evans.

Usage
-----

  python3 vhmodesgen.py --vh VH-TKV      # also accepts VHTKV or TKV
  vh-tkv : 7c61ad

  python3 vhmodesgen.py -s 7c61ad
  7c61ad : VH-TKV

  python3 vhmodesgen.py --all            # every address 7c0000-7cffff

-s only converts addresses in 7c0000-7cb63f (VH-AAA to VH-999). Anything else,
or an invalid mark given to --vh, prints a message and exits with status 1.
--all still walks the whole 7c0000-7cffff range, as described in the notes at
the top of vhmodesgen.py.

The functions can be imported (import vhmodesgen) without running the command line.

Checking Mode S / ADS-B frames
------------------------------

modes_frame.py checks whether a received frame belongs to a VH- aircraft:

  python3 modes_frame.py 8D7C61AD2150B5A0820820B9C954 VH-TKV
  DF17 AA=7C61AD (VH-TKV) parity OK, TC=4, flight ID 'TKV', emitter A1 -> MATCHES VH-TKV (7C61AD)

It checks the CRC, reads the address from DF11/DF17, recovers it from the
Address/Parity field of DF0/4/5/16/20/21, and for DF17 identification messages
compares the flight ID with the registration. An address recovered from a short
reply isn't proof on its own: a corrupted DF4/DF5 gives a different address
rather than a failed check, so look for a DF11 or DF17 with good parity.

  python3 modes_frame.py --examples      # synthetic test frames for VH-TKV

The encoders (DF4, DF5, DF11, DF17 TC 4/9-18/19/31) build test frames; they are
checked against pyModeS in the tests. modes_frame.py itself needs only the
standard library.

Tests
-----

  python3 -m unittest -v test_vhmodesgen

The pyModeS cross-check runs only if pyModeS 3.x is installed (pip install pyModeS).
